        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic shows the organisation at the centre ringed by six labelled segments — Political, Economic, Social, Technological, Environmental, Legal. Use the ring to make two points: the forces act on the firm from outside its control, and they interact with each other. In application, have students annotate each segment with concrete, industry- relevant trends and then star the few that qualify as key drivers of change.",
        "boundaryTrap": "**Boundary Trap & Novice Anti-Pattern**: • For short-horizon operational decisions — macro trends move too slowly to inform quarterly choices\n• As a competitor or industry analysis — PESTEL scans the macro layer; use Five Forces for industry structure\n• When it degenerates into an unprioritised list of trends with no link to the specific business decision\n• In isolation for entry decisions — it identifies conditions, not whether the firm can win there",
