        "frameworkBreakdown": "**TAM / SAM / SOM (Part III — Go-to-Market Strategy)**: Market sizing proceeds through three nested estimates. TAM (Total Addressable Market): the full revenue opportunity if every potential customer of the product category were captured — the outer bound. SAM (Serviceable Addressable Market): the portion of TAM reachable with your actual product, geography, channel and regulatory scope. SOM (Serviceable Obtainable Market): the share of SAM realistically winnable in a planning horizon given competition, capacity and go-to-market strength — the number a revenue plan should rest on. Two estimation routes should triangulate: top-down (industry reports sliced by filters) and bottom-up (number of target customers × realistic price × plausible penetration). Bottom-up is more credible because it exposes assumptions; top- down alone invites the '1% of a huge market' fallacy.",
