        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic is the standard nine-block layout: Key Partnerships, Key Activities, Key Resources on the left; Value Propositions centre; Customer Relationships, Channels, Customer Segments on the right; Cost Structure and Revenue Streams as the two base blocks. Teach the geography: right side = value creation for the market, left side = value delivery machinery, bottom = the economic equation. Have students draw arrows between blocks that must cohere — the arrows expose the model's logic and its fractures.",
