        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic is a 2×2 grid: columns split Helpful vs Harmful factors, rows split Internal vs External origin, yielding Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats. When teaching, extend it into the TOWS matching matrix — SO, WO, ST, WT strategy cells — to show students that the grid is the input, and the strategies generated from pairings are the output.",
        "boundaryTrap": "**Boundary Trap & Novice Anti-Pattern**: • As the primary analysis — SWOT is a synthesis of deeper work, not a source of insight on its own\n• When items cannot be evidenced or benchmarked against competitors ('good quality' is opinion, not analysis)\n• For prioritisation decisions — the grid ranks nothing; ten unweighted strengths give no guidance\n• When internal politics will censor the W and T cells — an unhonest SWOT is worse than none",
