    "title": "THE PATENDED PHARMA MOAT",
    "track": "fmcg-brand",
    "sector": "Corporate Strategy",
    "company": "Enterprise Case",
    "context": "A pharmaceutical startup develops a molecule that cures baldness (Valuable). They hold a 20-year patent (Rare and Inimitable). However, they lack the manufacturing facilities, distribution networks, and marketing expertise to commercialize the drug, leaving the patent sitting in their vault.",
    "prompt": "Under VRIO, what is the current strategic status of the startup's molecule?",
