        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic is a 2×2: horizontal axis = source of advantage (lower cost vs differentiation), vertical axis = competitive scope (broad vs narrow). Broad row yields Cost Leadership and Differentiation; narrow row yields Cost Focus and Differentiation Focus. Draw 'stuck in the middle' as the void at the centre. Ask students to place 8–10 named firms on the grid and defend the placements — misplacements reveal the concept gaps.",
        "boundaryTrap": "**Boundary Trap & Novice Anti-Pattern**: 15\n• When the business genuinely competes on a hybrid model with proven economics — forcing a label obscures reality\n• For corporate-level (multi-business) strategy — the framework addresses how one business unit competes\n• In winner-take-all digital markets where scale and network effects, not cost-vs-differentiation choice, decide outcomes\n• As a static, one-time choice — positions must be revisited as technology shifts the cost of differentiation",
