    "sector": "Corporate Strategy",
    "company": "Enterprise Case",
    "context": "The soft drink concentrate industry (Coca-Cola, Pepsi) has structurally generated high ROIC (>30%) for decades. Concentrate makers sell to independent bottlers who face high capital costs for bottling plants and have exclusive territory contracts, meaning they cannot switch to alternative brands.",
    "prompt": "Under Porter's Five Forces, which structural element best explains the high profitability of concentrate manufacturers?",
