    "sector": "Corporate Strategy",
    "company": "Enterprise Case",
    "context": "A large e-commerce retailer integrates its automated sorting conveyor belts (Operations) with its inventory database (Inbound/Outbound Logistics). As soon as an item is scanned on arrival, the system maps the optimal storage shelf and pre-assigns it to an outbound courier van.",
    "prompt": "In Porter's Value Chain, how does this integration create a competitive cost advantage?",
