        "justification": "Suboptimal strategic move: violates core unit economics or misjudges competitive dynamics.",
        "frameworkBreakdown": "**Marketing Mix: 4Ps / 7Ps (Part II — Marketing Strategy)**: McCarthy's 4Ps organise the controllable levers of marketing execution: Product (features, quality, design, packaging, service, brand), Price (list price, discounts, terms — the only P that generates rather than spends revenue), Place (channels, coverage, logistics, inventory) and Promotion (advertising, sales force, PR, digital, sales promotion). Booms and Bitner extended the mix to 7Ps for services, adding People (staff who deliver the experience), Process (service delivery flows and queues) and Physical Evidence (tangible cues — environment, design, documents — that signal invisible quality.) The mix is not a checklist but a consistency test: every P must reinforce the same STP choices, and the Ps must cohere with each other — premium product with discount pricing signals confusion.",
        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic shows the target customer at the centre with the four Ps as quadrants around it — Product, Price, Place, Promotion — and the three service Ps (People, Process, Physical Evidence) as an outer ring. The centre placement is deliberate pedagogy: every lever is set with reference to the chosen target, and the outer ring signals the service extension rather than a separate model.",
