    "sector": "Corporate Strategy",
    "company": "Enterprise Case",
    "context": "A SaaS startup hosts its application on AWS. Last year, AWS increased hosting rates by 15%, squeezing the startup's gross margins. The startup's database architecture is tightly coupled with AWS-proprietary services (DynamoDB, Redshift), meaning migrating to Google Cloud would take 8 months of rewrite and $250,000 in migration costs.",
    "prompt": "Under Porter's Five Forces, what does this migration barrier represent?",
