        "frameworkBreakdown": "**Related vs. Unrelated Diversification (Part I — Business Strategy)**: This framework analyzes the performance implications of Related Diversification (sharing value chain links or channels) vs. Unrelated Diversification (expanding with no operational synergies, operating as a conglomerate). In developed markets, unrelated diversification leads to a Conglomerate Discount due to efficient capital markets and specialist firms. In emerging markets, Institutional Voids (weak capital markets, logistics, or legal frameworks) allow diversified conglomerates to earn a Conglomerate Premium by acting as efficient internal intermediaries for capital, talent, and brand trust.",
        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic acts as a contextual filter. When passing a diversification decision through the institutional voids filter, the outcome changes: in developed markets, unrelated diversification leads to a Conglomerate Discount; in emerging markets, institutional voids enable conglomerates to capture a Conglomerate Premium by acting as internal intermediaries.",
        "boundaryTrap": "**Boundary Trap & Novice Anti-Pattern**: • For assessing startup business plans (startups lack the scale to build internal markets)\n• For short-term financial trading or options valuation\n• In markets that have transitioned from emerging to developed where voids have closed",
