        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic is a 3×3 grid: industry attractiveness (low→high) on the vertical axis, competitive strength (weak→strong) on the horizontal. Shade the three top-right cells 'Invest/Grow', the three diagonal cells 'Selectivity/Earnings', the three bottom-left 'Harvest/Divest'. In class, add weighted-score tables beside each axis so students see the machinery behind a unit's placement, then perturb one weight to show how placements move.",
