        "isCorrect": true,
        "justification": "**Analysis**: Customer satisfaction is non-linear. In financial services, security, login reliability, and transfer speed are non-negotiable threshold baselines. If baseline hygiene features fail, users experience severe dissatisfaction regardless of how many AI delighters are added.  **Framework Application**: Framework: The Kano Model (Kano) Utilization: The consultant plots engineering backlog items on the **Kano Grid** (Customer Satisfaction vs Feature Execution): (1) **Must-Be / Baseline (Threshold)**: biometric authentication, security, sub-second transfer latency - these do not create delight when working, but cause catastrophic dissatisfaction when broken; (2) **One-Dimensional (Performance)**: app speed, transaction search; (3) **Attractive (Delighters)**: AI insights, gamified cashback. The Kano rule is absolute: **Delighters cannot compensate for failing Must-Be baselines**.  **Boundary Trap to Avoid**: Building shiny delighter features while core baseline functionality is broken. THE STRATEGY BOARDROOM  -  COMPLETE CASE CURRICULUM Confidential  MBA Teaching Series  Abridged Edition  --- PAGE 22 ---  ---",
