        "frameworkUtilization": "How to read it. How to read it. The schematic is the classic arrow: the bottom band shows the five primary activities flowing left to right toward Margin at the arrowhead; the upper bands show the four support activities stretching across all primary activities to signal that they enable the whole chain. In teaching, have students write each activity's cost share and its contribution to buyer value — the asymmetries revealed are where strategy discussions start.",
        "boundaryTrap": "**Boundary Trap & Novice Anti-Pattern**: 13\n• For startups with little activity structure yet — there is no chain to disaggregate before product–market fit\n• When cost data cannot be allocated to activities — without numbers the chain becomes a decorative org chart\n• As a substitute for customer analysis — the chain shows where value is made, not what buyers value\n• In pure platform businesses where value is created by network participants, not a linear activity sequence — adapt or use a different lens",
