    "id": 802,
    "title": "THE RETIRED BROWSER TRANSITION",
    "track": "tech-pm",
    "sector": "Corporate Strategy",
    "company": "Enterprise Case",
    "context": "Microsoft's legacy Internet Explorer browser once had 95% market share but entered a low-growth, declining market. Microsoft milked the ad revenue from Internet Explorer for years to fund the early development of Azure Cloud Services (high growth, low share at the time).",
